## Implementation Spec: Phase Settings Mobile Responsiveness

### Task 1: Add responsive CSS media queries to `server/templates/client.html`

**File:** `server/templates/client.html`
**Approach:** Add CSS media queries in the `<style>` section (after the existing styles, before the closing `</style>` tag).

**CSS to add:**

```css
@media (max-width: 768px) {
  body {
    padding: 1rem;
  }

  #agent-status {
    flex-direction: column !important;
  }

  .settings-row {
    flex-direction: column !important;
    align-items: stretch !important;
    gap: 0.5rem !important;
    padding: 0.75rem 0 !important;
  }

  .settings-row .phase-label {
    min-width: unset !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }

  .settings-row .phase-agent,
  .settings-row .phase-model {
    flex: unset !important;
    width: 100% !important;
    min-height: 44px !important;
    padding: 0.5rem !important;
    font-size: 16px !important;
  }

  .settings-row .save-phase-btn {
    width: 100% !important;
    min-height: 44px !important;
    padding: 0.5rem !important;
    font-size: 0.9rem !important;
  }
}

@media (max-width: 480px) {
  body {
    padding: 0.75rem;
  }

  .settings-grid {
    padding: 0.5rem !important;
  }

  h1 {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
  }

  h2 {
    font-size: 1rem;
  }
}
```

**Dependencies:** None. This is the only task.

**Details:**
- `!important` declarations are needed because existing styles are inline (`style=` attributes on elements at lines 294-303), and CSS media queries in `<style>` have lower specificity than inline styles.
- `font-size: 16px` on inputs/selects prevents Safari iOS from auto-zooming when focusing form fields (Safari zooms if font-size < 16px).
- `min-height: 44px` ensures all interactive elements meet Apple Human Interface Guidelines for minimum touch target size.
- `flex-direction: column` on `.settings-row` converts the horizontal layout (label + select + input + button in a row) to a vertical stack on mobile.
- `align-items: stretch` ensures all children expand to full container width.
- The `#agent-status` flex-direction change is a bonus fix — the two agent cards also overflow on narrow screens since they use `flex:1` side by side.

**Where to insert:** Find the closing `</style>` tag in the `<head>` section. The styles start at line 13. Add the media queries just before `</style>`.

**What NOT to change:**
- Do not modify any HTML structure or element ordering
- Do not modify any JavaScript
- Do not change desktop layout (all changes are inside media queries)
- Do not move the Phase Settings section in the DOM

### Verification

1. Open the client page in Chrome DevTools responsive mode
2. At 768px width and below: phase settings rows should stack vertically with full-width controls
3. At 480px width: additional padding/font adjustments for very narrow screens
4. At desktop widths (>768px): layout should be completely unchanged
5. All Save buttons should still function correctly
6. No horizontal scrolling at any viewport width
